00:46:20,869 --> 00:46:26,869
The film stars Mike Myers as the Cat in the Hat, alongside Alec
Baldwin, Kelly Preston, Dakota Fanning, and Spencer Breslin.

14
00:49:54,782 --> 00:50:00,782
Directed by Bo Welch and written by Alec Berg, David Mandel, and Jeff Schaffer, it follows siblings Sally and Conrad Walden getting paid a visit
by the Cat in the Hat, who plans to lighten up their rainy day with fun activities, while their mother Joan is at the office.

15
00:53:28,695 --> 00:53:34,695
All the while, Larry Quinn, the Walden's sleazy next-door neighbor, plans to send
Conrad to military school and mooch off of Joan for her wealth.

16
00:57:02,608 --> 00:57:08,608
Produced by Imagine Entertainment, The Cat in the Hat premiered in Universal City, California, on November 8, 2003, and was released
in theaters in the United States on November 21 by Universal Pictures, and internationally by DreamWorks Pictures.

17
01:00:36,521 --> 01:00:42,521
The film received overwhelmingly negative reviews from critics and was a box-office
disappointment, grossing $134 million worldwide on a budget of $109 million.

18
01:04:10,434 --> 01:04:16,434
It was nominated for ten awards at the 24th Golden Raspberry
Awards, including Worst Picture and Worst Director.

19
01:07:44,347 --> 01:07:50,347
The negative reception of the film led to Seuss's widow, Audrey Geisel, prohibiting any further live-action
adaptations of her husband's books, including a planned sequel based on The Cat in the Hat Comes Back.

20
01:11:18,260 --> 01:11:24,260
An animated readaptation is scheduled for release on November 6, 2026.

21
01:14:52,173 --> 01:14:58,173
The film explores themes of sibling relationship,
chaos, cat, boredom, surrealism.

